Ds are closed and reservation is not admission; native-executable-only artifact/launcher model is coherent for Rust, Swift and Kotlin Native; local source-root rules and external skill-build.json schema evolution remain package-command-free; signing/platform/hardened claims stay honest. Cross-check against parallel TASK-260728-1g0z69: decision 0008 says descriptor schema 2 changes exactly one thing and adds no member, while the toolchain contract expects next-schema manifest and potentially descriptor requirements. Flag any contradiction that would make TASK-260728-251p01 impossible or force undocumented schema evolution. Check whether generalizing manager-worker-v1 process/session semantics is truly semantic preservation or needs v2; whether receipt 3/4 by source mode is unambiguous; all schemas 1-7 and rc.5 bytes must remain unchanged. Re-run focused guards, negative probes, deterministic/release gates; do not stage, commit, publish, pin, or claim native platforms.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-49e194, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-49e194)\nReview logbook 2026-07-28 — CHANGES REQUESTED and routed to analysis. Independent validation is green: 42 schemas / 422 vectors, 44 Python tests, 15 focused boundary tests, Go tests/vet/format, diff check, clean deterministic regeneration, and rc.5 release gate. Blocking contract defects remain: decision 0008 excludes the required manifest and optional descriptor toolchain requirement from the exact next-schema shapes; it widens the frozen Go-specific manager-worker-v1 identity into a generic policy without versioning; it says six identifiers are both admitted and merely reserved;