12 lines) plus tools/validate.py and tools/test_validate.py; still exactly three files different from the accepted TASK-260728-2kp3tv base. (1) Toolchain placement reconciled with decision 0007: reserved definitions buildCommandV8 and repositoryBuildCommandV2 carry a REQUIRED closed toolchain-requirement-v1 member, skillBuildTargetV2 carries it OPTIONAL, and buildCommandV6/repositoryBuildCommandV1/skillBuildTargetV1 are frozen and may never gain it; section 8 records why the REQUIRED member changes no go-v1 identity (the requirement is a gate, not a build input). (2) manager-worker-v1 left frozen and Go-only; manager-worker-v2 minted for the six reserved drivers as a concurrent sibling with an identical containment contract, an explicit non-ordering rule, and a closed driver-to-policy table made structural in claim schema 4. Knock-on capability-evidence-v2 reserved because v1 is closed to one policy and one record per operation while schema 8 admits mixed operations. The earlier claim that a new policy identity would invalidate rc.5 was false and is corrected. (3) Section 2 split into a named Admitted wire driver set (go-v1, go-repository-v1 only) and a named Reserved driver namespace (the six), with a single atomic transition owned by TASK-260728-251p01; both labels are gate-required terms. (4) Gate deny-lists replaced with closed exact member-set tables covering deployed, reserved and manager-authored driver-bearing definitions, plus a residual never-legal-name deny-list; all three demonstrated false accepts (optional language on buildCommandV6, arbitrary command on skillBuildTargetV1, runtime_files on buildRecordV2) now reject. Reserved-name absence scan extended to manager-worker-v2; capability-evidence-v2 deliberately excluded because that literal already appears in the frozen rc.5 corpus and release gate as the rejected example, so non-admission is proved positively instead, and the two literals TASK-260728-251p01 must move at rc.6 are named in the decision. Gates green standalone with the task venv: validate.py 0 (42 schemas / 422 files), unittest 0 (60 tests, was 44), go test 0, go vet 0, gofmt 0, compileall 0, git diff --check 0. Clean-checkout probe at commit 92cf7a5: make validate 0, make regenerate-check 0 twice, make release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.5 0. rc.5 preserved: manifest digest sha256:9ba9b8ecf6f06cafda1425aed3539dee8d12af43dabd36f803f4f420dbb1dacf unchanged, release/1.0.0-rc.5.json unchanged, two regenerations byte-identical. CLI plant-and-revert probes confirmed rejection of manager-worker-v2 on protocol/core.md and of toolchain added to the frozen skillBuildTargetV1, both files restored byte-identical. Nothing staged, committed, published, pinned, or claimed; no platform or native validation claim. Housekeeping: a stray .venv left inside the worktree by the previous cycle was removed. Board artifact note: TASK-260728-2spy93_decision-0008-... is the current decision; the older TASK-260728-2spy93_decision-0007-... attachment is a stale pre-renumber duplicate of the same file and could not be deleted because task-board resource delete aborts on an unrelated board element carrying an unparseable status value todo.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-fc2e6b, pid=31330, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 2 directive 2026-07-28: independently verify all four prior blocking findings against the final rework. Confirm schema-8 local and repository commands carry REQUIRED toolchain and descriptor-v2 target carries OPTIONAL toolchain while every frozen v1/v6/v7 shape stays exact; manager-worker-v1 remains Go-only and byte/semantic frozen, with manager-worker-v2 reserved only for the six new drivers and no Go cache-key change; capability-evidence-v2 reservation is coherent despite the rc.5 negative fixture already containing that rejected literal and remains unadmitted; admitted-wire and reserved-namespace sets are disjoint with one atomic transition; exact close